  - image: {fileID: 3223091865968251079, guid: 65557a665b966b642b04621316fa8e4e, type: 3}
    description: The NAND gate is the opposite of the AND gate. It outputs 0 only
      when all inputs are 1. It is also known as a universal gate because any other
      logic gate (AND, OR, NOT, etc.) can be constructed using only NAND gates.
